        "acceptedPr": null,
        "calls": 1,
        "title": "Base agent spawn gating skips non-spawning workers",
        "summary": "The `loadAgentDefinitions` function in `cli/src/utils/local-agent-registry.ts` now gates auto-added user agents to base agents that actually support spawning, checking for `spawn_agents`, `spawn_agent_inline` tool names, or a `handleSteps` definition. Previously, any agent with an ID starting with 'base' and a `spawnableAgents` field received user agents appended, which could incorrectly add children to non-spawning worker agents that share the 'base' id prefix. The new test 'custom agents do not make bundled fast-mode workers fail validation' asserts that `base3-fast-worker-deepseek-flash` and its evals variant keep an empty `spawnableAgents` list and lack `spawn_agents` in `toolNames`.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "audience": "end-users",
        "evidence": "In `cli/src/utils/local-agent-registry.ts`, the `loadAgentDefinitions` function's loop that auto-adds user agent IDs to `spawnableAgents` now checks `def.toolNames?.includes('spawn_agents') || def.toolNames?.includes('spawn_agent_inline') || def.handleSteps` before adding, with the comment 'Non-spawning workers also start with base; keep their child list empty.'",
